<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσ-κρουσμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that against which one strikes, obstacle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				658a7
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>knock,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hippiatr.
				96
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stumblingblock, cause of offence</i> or <i>friction</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				54.3
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				1.26.3
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιτικὰ π. τοῖς δημάρχοις πρὸς τοὺς
					ὑπάτους συνέστη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					10.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.25
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ περὶ τὴν σιτοδοσίαν
			π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.45
			</span></i>.—The form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσκρουμα</span></b>  (which is preferred by Thom.Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.317
			</span></i> R., citing <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				1.455
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>) freq. occurs in the same Mss. as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσκρουσμα</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.137c
			</span></i> with <i><span class="en">
				141b
			</span></i>, al.</div>
